WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.330
Strip away all the fierce makeup, battle-coiffed
hairstyles, and intricate tattoos, and the

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:10.190
Norse warriors on Vikings are just like the
rest of us...if we were all muscular and ridiculously

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.080
good looking, anyway.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:15.351
Sure, their characters look like they'd fit
right into the Viking Age of history, but

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.780
here's what these 21st-century actors look
like in real life.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.340
Travis Fimmel

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:25.480
Though he doesn't sport Ragnar's shaved head
and ZZ Top beard in real life, Travis Fimmel

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.580
still looks pretty Vikingly, with a blonde
beard and striking blue eyes.

00:00:29.749 --> 00:00:33.359
The actor and model doesn't actually hail
from the northlands of Scandinavia, though.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.580
Rather, he comes from down under, and was
raised on his family's farm in Australia.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.280
Fimmel is set to write and produce a scripted
anthology series for the History Channel detailing

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:47.750
the stories of some of history's biggest anti-heroes,
and is set to star as the gunslingin' Wyatt

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.840
Earp on the new series' first episode.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.720
Katheryn Winnick

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.440
It's easy to argue that Katheryn Winnick is
the most iconically Viking-looking actor on

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:01.240
the entire show, even if she doesn't really
hail from Scandinavia—she's actually Canadian.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.540
And Winnick doesn't only kick ass on TV.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:08.530
The actress has been training in martial arts
since childhood, and boasts some serious credentials.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:09.680
Winnick told StarPulse:

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.680
"I got into my first [martial arts] school
when I was 16.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:17.340
I have a 3rd degree black belt in Tae Kwon
Do and a 2nd degree black belt in Karate."

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.620
She's also a licensed bodyguard and self-defense
instructor.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.620
So don't mess with Earl Ingstad.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:24.900
Alexander Ludwig

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:30.060
Over the course of the show's run, Vikings
fans have watched Ragnar Lothbrok's firstborn

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:33.240
son grow up from a momma's boy to a bear-killing
warrior.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:38.000
As his character has aged, we've seen actor
Alexander Ludwig's look transition from short

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.700
hair and and a peach fuzz beard to a shaved
head with one extra-long, braided ponytail.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:47.200
In real life, Ludwig keeps a beard going,
though he doesn't walk around California with

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.900
a waist-long Viking ponytail.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:53.160
Though Ludwig obviously didn't play the child
version of Björn in the show, he has been

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.660
acting since he was a child.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:59.540
Most notably, Ludwig took home an MTV Movie
Award for Best Fight thanks to his role as

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.260
Cato in The Hunger Games.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:02.720
Clive Standen

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:07.580
Rollo is one of the most fearsome Vikings
on the show, and he always looked the part,

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:09.760
with long, dark hair and a bushy beard.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.140
In real life, however, Clive Standen looks
less ferocious, as he tends to stay sharp

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:17.010
with short, tidy hair and a finely-trimmed
beard.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:19.300
But don't let that clean-shaven appearance
fool you.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:24.020
The actor has been riding horses, jousting
and sword fighting since childhood, and is

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:29.000
also a Muay Thai expert — meaning you wouldn't
want to challenge Standen on any battlefield,

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:29.600
Viking or not.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.280
Gustaf Skarsgård

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:36.820
As his name implies, Gustaf Skarsgård is
one of Vikings' only true Scandinavians, though

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.880
he looks a lot less fearsome in real life.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.780
While Flóki is famous for sporting a beard
and that iconic crying makeup, Skarsgård

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.640
stays clean-shaven and professional, just
like the rest of his actor-filled family.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.140
It's a big family, too.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:53.780
His father, Stellan Skarsgård, is easily
the most famous of the family, having appeared

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:58.310
in Good Will Hunting, the Pirates of the Caribbean
franchise, The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo,

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.300
and the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:05.260
You may also know Gustaf's brother, Alexander
Skarsgård, for his roles as Eric Northman

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:10.220
in HBO's long-running series True Blood and
the title character in The Legend of Tarzan.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:14.640
And chances are, you know his other brother,
Bill, thanks to his performance as Pennywise

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:15.980
in Stephen King's It.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.240
That's one seriously prolific family.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:19.960
Alyssa Sutherland

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:25.040
In the role of Queen Aslaug, Alyssa Sutherland
can bewitch even a Viking king with her stunning

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.540
looks — a trait to be expected in a famous,
real-life fashion model.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:33.180
Sutherland got her modeling start when Cadbury
revived its iconic "Flake Girl" advertising

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:33.680
campaign.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:38.360
She's since been featured in campaigns for
such brands as Calvin Klein and Chanel , among

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:38.860
others.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:42.940
Not many models make the successful transition
to acting like Sutherland already has, so

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:46.860
we'll have to wait and see if this Vikings
star lands more prime roles in the future.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:48.600
Maude Hirst

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:53.800
With her long blonde hair and kind face, Maude
Hirst was a perfect casting choice for Helga,

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:56.800
the wife of Flóki, though she undoubtedly
had some help.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:02.100
Her father is Michael Hirst, the writer and
producer of Elizabeth, The Tudors and Vikings.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:05.620
Hirst doesn't credit her father for getting
her into the acting biz, though.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:06.940
She told View of the Arts:

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.050
"I was always creative, I didn't grow up much
with my father.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:14.330
I was raised by my mum who is an artist and
that's what probably influenced my creativity."

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:18.269
While there's no doubt Hirst deserves the
role of Helga, it certainly never hurts to

00:04:18.269 --> 00:04:20.180
have your father as the show's producer.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:21.900
Linus Roache

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:26.600
Give him a crown, and Linus Roache looks almost
identical to King Ecbert in real life.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:31.500
Aside from Vikings, most television viewers
probably know him best as Michael Cutter in

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.460
the long-running crime drama Law &amp; Order.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:38.240
On top of all that, Roache has also made quite
a few big screen appearances, with roles in

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.080
Priest, Batman Begins, and The Chronicles
of Riddick, among others.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:43.600
Moe Dunford

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:48.780
Though he plays the English Prince Aethelwulf
in Vikings, actor Moe Dunford is actually

00:04:48.789 --> 00:04:53.590
Irish — a fact slightly masked by the show's
producers, who've given the character dark

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:56.120
brown hair rather than Dunford's natural red.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:01.060
Irish audiences, however, are certainly inclined
to recognize Dunford as the actor who played

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:05.490
Patrick Fitzgerald in Patrick's Day — an
award-winning Irish drama centered around

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:09.940
a 26-year-old schizophrenic and his St. Patrick's
Day disappearance in Dublin.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:10.920
Jennie Jacques

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:17.140
Take Vikings' Judith out of her medieval princess
garb and stick her in some 21st-century clothes,

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.659
and you have actress Jennie Jacques.

00:05:18.659 --> 00:05:23.419
Besides a wardrobe change and some makeup,
very little seems to be done to actually change

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.900
Jacques' appearance for the show.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:27.780
Jacques is no stranger to the historical drama.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:32.480
Fans may recognize the actress from her other
major role as Annie Miller in the BBC series

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:33.720
Desperate Romantics.

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:38.780
She's also an advocate for epilepsy awareness
and recently completed an open water swim

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:42.700
and a Spartan Sprint to raise money for the
Epilepsy Society.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:44.720
Alex Andersen

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:50.139
Like his character Ivar the Boneless, Alex
Andersen almost never sports a beard.

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:53.520
Unlike his character, however, he looks a
lot less scary in real life.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:57.260
And as you probably guessed, Andersen's legs
work just fine.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:02.100
Aside from Vikings, Andersen also appeared
in the Danish drama A War, which received

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:06.180
a nomination for the Best Foreign Language
Film at the 88th Academy Awards.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:07.800
John Kavanagh

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:12.260
You probably won't recognize Vikings' The
Seer from anywhere, considering the blind

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:17.110
oracle is covered in an extensive amount of
makeup, has no eyes, and is most frequently

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.779
portrayed in his dark hut.

00:06:18.779 --> 00:06:23.069
John Kavanagh obviously doesn't look grotesque
in real life, which may be why you missed

00:06:23.069 --> 00:06:25.940
the fact that he also played the Pope in a
Season 4 episode.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:29.260
Now that you know what he looks like, you
might recognize Kavanagh from The Tudors,

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:33.500
as well as minor roles in bigger films like
The Black Dahlia and Braveheart.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:38.240
Whether or not Kavanagh enjoys having his
palm regularly licked by Vikings' stars, however,

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:40.040
is best left to speculation.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:41.360
Thanks for watching!

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.220
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.740
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

